K. Known Limitations
--------------------

1. No adaptation.  No ghost lists, no frequency tracking beyond the
   binary cool/hot flag.  Cannot detect or respond to workload phase
   changes.

2. No VACUUM integration.  hint_vacuum is NULL.  VACUUM-loaded pages
   enter the cache as "hot" and must survive a full clock cycle before
   eviction.

3. No prefetch integration.  prefetch_hint is NULL.  No pre-cooling or
   pre-warming of pages that are about to be accessed.

4. Binary cool/hot is coarser than PostgreSQL's usage_count (0-5) or
   ARC's explicit list ordering.  Frequently accessed pages get the same
   protection as pages accessed only once.

5. on_miss stat attribution to partition 0 is imprecise.  At miss time
   the buffer ID is not yet known, so the miss cannot be attributed to
   the correct partition.  This is a minor reporting issue.

6. osic_partition_for_buf() uses a linear scan of partitions.  This
   could be replaced with arithmetic (local_id / bufs_per_part) if
   partitions were guaranteed to be equal-sized.  With at most 16
   partitions the linear scan is negligible, but the arithmetic
   approach would be cleaner.


L. Future Work
--------------

1. Multi-bit cool counter.  Replace the single cool flag with a 2-bit
   or 3-bit usage counter (similar to PostgreSQL's usage_count) for
   finer eviction granularity.  This would give frequently accessed
   pages more protection while keeping the lock-free atomic hit path.

2. VACUUM hint.  Implement hint_vacuum to set the cool flag immediately
   on VACUUM-loaded pages, making them the first eviction candidates
   after a single clock sweep.  This would prevent VACUUM from polluting
   the cache.

3. Prefetch hint.  Implement prefetch_hint to pre-cool pages that are
   about to be replaced.  When the buffer manager signals an upcoming
   load, the target buffer's cool flag could be set proactively, reducing
   eviction latency.

4. Arithmetic partition lookup.  If partition sizes are made exactly
   equal (with a possible small unused remainder), osic_partition_for_buf
   could use division instead of a linear scan.
